{"name":"Menacing Clouds","hex":"#69788a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"menacing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of threatening in its various senses."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of menace"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/menacing"},{"term":"clouds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of cloud"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of cloud"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clouds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Menacing","blocks":[{"text":"Menacing, brandishment or brandishing are criminal offenses in many U.S. states consisting of displaying a weapon with the intent of placing another person in fear of imminent physical injury or death."},{"text":"The term \"brandish\" means, with respect to a firearm, to display all or part of the firearm, or otherwise make the presence of the firearm known to another person, in order to intimidate that person, regardless of whether the firearm is directly visible to that person. — 18 U.S.C. § 924(c)(4)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menacing","wikidata":"Q6816390"},{"title":"Cloud","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, a cloud is an aerosol consisting of a visible mass of miniature liquid droplets, ice crystals, or other particles, suspended in the atmosphere of a planetary body or similar space. Water, primarily, comprises the droplets and crystals. On Earth, clouds are formed as a result of saturation of the air when it is cooled to its dew point, or when it gains sufficient moisture, usually in the form of water vapor, from an adjacent source to raise the dew point to the ambient temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg/330px-ISS-40_Thunderheads_near_Borneo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud","wikidata":"Q8074"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/500px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/1280px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Dreamy_Twilight.jpg/500px-Dreamy_Twilight.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Windy evening twilight enhanced by the Sun's angle. Clouds can visually mimic a tornado resulting from orographic lift.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADreamy_Twilight.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cirrus-fibratus.jpg/500px-Cirrus-fibratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cirrus-fibratus.jpg/1280px-Cirrus-fibratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cirrus-fibratus.jpg/500px-Cirrus-fibratus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cirrus fibratus clouds in March","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACirrus-fibratus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cirrus_sky_panorama.jpg/500px-Cirrus_sky_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cirrus_sky_panorama.jpg/1280px-Cirrus_sky_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cirrus_sky_panorama.jpg/500px-Cirrus_sky_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai